| Type                     | Returns                          | Common Operators                |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Single-Row Subquery      | One row                          | `=`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `<>` |
| Multiple-Row Subquery    | Multiple rows                    | `IN`, `ANY`, `ALL`, `EXISTS`    |
| Multiple-Column Subquery | Multiple columns                 | `IN`, row comparisons           |
| Correlated Subquery      | Depends on outer query           | `EXISTS`, comparison operators  |
| Non-Correlated Subquery  | Independent                      | Any valid operator              |
| Nested Subquery          | Subquery within another subquery | Any valid operator              |


EXISTS is a SQL operator used to check whether a subquery returns at least one row.


select * from customers where age > (select avg(age) from customers);

select * from customers where age > any
 ( select age from customers where country = "USA");

select * from customers where (age,country) in
 ( select age ,country from customers where first_name like "john");

select * from customers c where age <
 (select sum(amount) from orders o where o.customer_id=c.customer_id);  // depends on outer query 


SELECT name
FROM Employees
WHERE department_id = (
    SELECT department_id
    FROM Departments
    WHERE manager_id = (
        SELECT employee_id
        FROM Employees
        WHERE name = 'John'
    )
);
